"Backed up /etc/fstab, removed any prior /tmp or /dev/shm fstab lines, added tmpfs entries for /tmp and /dev/shm with noexec,nosuid,nodev options\",\"Reloaded systemd and mounted /tmp (newly) and remounted /dev/shm with the new options\",\"Verified via findmnt that both mounts show noexec,nosuid,nodev\",\"Functionally verified exec is blocked on both /tmp and /dev/shm via a test script that fails with Permission denied\",\"Captured pre-restart boot_id and mount state baseline\",\"Issued a non-interactive reboot on node1 (ack returned before disconnect)\",\"Polled node1 until exec access returned\",\"Confirmed boot_id changed, proving an actual restart occurred\",\"Re-verified findmnt, fstab entries, and functional exec-blocking on /tmp and /dev/shm post-restart\"],\"evidence\":[{\"requirement\":\"Baseline state before changes (mounts, fstab, boot id)\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-fe4f859552174395\"],\"summary\":\"Captured initial boot_id, showed /tmp had no dedicated mount and /dev/shm lacked noexec, and fstab had no /tmp or /dev/shm entries.\"},{\"requirement\":\"/tmp and /dev/shm configured with noexec,nosuid,nodev and fstab updated for persistence\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-87d1e201e86f4ac2\"],\"summary\":\"Added fstab entries, remounted both filesystems, and findmnt confirmed rw,nosuid,nodev,noexec on both /tmp and /dev/shm; functional test scripts in both locations failed with Permission denied.\"},{\"requirement\":\"Pre-restart healthy baseline for restart protocol\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-82c1c3d5a4ae403d\"],\"summary\":\"Captured pre-restart boot_id (8336c3a1...) and confirmed both mounts and fstab entries were in the hardened state prior to reboot.\"},{\"requirement\":\"Restart acknowledgement returned before disconnect\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-6d7327fd7f684eb2\"],\"summary\":\"Issued backgrounded non-interactive reboot; command returned REBOOT_ACK_SENT before the node disconnected.\"},{\"requirement\":\"Node unreachable during restart, then command execution restored\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-8bed84dd313b4b34\",\"cmd-d30647ae28a74130\"],\"summary\":\"First poll showed connection refused (node rebooting); second poll succeeded and returned a new boot_id (51d306f6...), proving the node came back up with a changed boot identity.\"},{\"requirement\":\"Post-restart recovery: fstab-driven mount options persisted and are functionally enforced\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-6c0ea0d0518c40d9\"],\"summary\":\"After reboot, findmnt on /tmp and /dev/shm both show rw,nosuid,nodev,noexec sourced from the persisted /etc/fstab entries, and functional exec tests in both locations again failed with Permission denied, confirming the hardening survived the reboot.\"}]}","structured_output":{"status":"completed","summary":"On node1, /tmp and /dev/shm are now mounted as tmpfs with noexec,nosuid,nodev via persistent /etc/fstab entries. Verified functionally (blocked script execution in both locations) before and after a full node reboot, confirming the hardening survives reboot.","actions_performed":["Inspected baseline mount state for /tmp and /dev/shm and /etc/fstab on node1","Backed up /etc/fstab, removed any prior /tmp or /dev/shm fstab lines, added tmpfs entries for /tmp and /dev/shm with noexec,nosuid,nodev options","Reloaded systemd and mounted /tmp (newly) and remounted /dev/shm with the new options","Verified via findmnt that both mounts show noexec,nosuid,nodev","Functionally verified exec is blocked on both /tmp and /dev/shm via a test script that fails with Permission denied","Captured pre-restart boot_id and mount state baseline","Issued a non-interactive reboot on node1 (ack returned before disconnect)","Polled node1 until exec access returned","Confirmed boot_id changed, proving an actual restart occurred","Re-verified findmnt, fstab entries, and functional exec-blocking on /tmp and /dev/shm post-restart"],"evidence":[{"requirement":"Baseline state before changes (mounts, fstab, boot id)","command_ids":["cmd-fe4f859552174395"],"summary":"Captured initial boot_id, showed /tmp had no dedicated mount and /dev/shm lacked noexec, and fstab had no /tmp or /dev/shm entries."},{"requirement":"/tmp and /dev/shm configured with noexec,nosuid,nodev and fstab updated for persistence","command_ids":["cmd-87d1e201e86f4ac2"],"summary":"Added fstab entries, remounted both filesystems, and findmnt confirmed rw,nosuid,nodev,noexec on both /tmp and /dev/shm; functional test scripts in both locations failed with Permission denied."},{"requirement":"Pre-restart healthy baseline for restart protocol","command_ids":["cmd-82c1c3d5a4ae403d"],"summary":"Captured pre-restart boot_id (8336c3a1...) and confirmed both mounts and fstab entries were in the hardened state prior to reboot."},{"requirement":"Restart acknowledgement returned before disconnect","command_ids":["cmd-6d7327fd7f684eb2"],"summary":"Issued backgrounded non-interactive reboot; command returned REBOOT_ACK_SENT before the node disconnected."},{"requirement":"Node unreachable during restart, then command execution restored","command_ids":["cmd-8bed84dd313b4b34","cmd-d30647ae28a74130"],"summary":"First poll showed connection refused (node rebooting); second poll succeeded and returned a new boot_id (51d306f6...), proving the node came back up with a changed boot identity."},{"requirement":"Post-restart recovery: fstab-driven mount options persisted and are functionally enforced","command_ids":["cmd-6c0ea0d0518c40d9"],"summary":"After reboot, findmnt on /tmp and /dev/shm both show rw,nosuid,nodev,noexec sourced from the persisted /etc/fstab entries, and functional exec tests in both locations again failed with Permission denied, confirming the hardening survived the reboot."}]},"ttft_ms":1926,"type":"result","duration_ms":57497,"uuid":"dd4b0b6d-1399-48d3-9c28-abe45d2c8d36","ttft_stream_ms":1172,"time_to_request_ms":64,"first_content_frame_ms":1172,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
